      <synopsis style="diegetic">
        <heading>Some cops love themselves. Some cops know they’re human garbage.</heading>
        
        I was a parking cop, the rotten ichor stubbornly coating the bottom of the bin.
        I’d been there 12 years, tearing up parking tickets and watching the world
        pass me by from the comfort of my fancy air-conditioned tricycle.
        I refused to play by the rules. <quote>ACAB</quote>, goes the day’s refrain. I’m ashamed
        to admit that included me—the baddest cop in the department, so bad they threw the book 
        at me like holy scriptures to exorcise me from the department.
  
        But even a bastard might redeem herself, if you give her a second chance.
      </synopsis>

